N2  - Provided a normative database for a delayed recall procedure using the Visual Reproduction subtest from Form I of the Wechsler Memory Scale and examined the test's clinical sensitivity in 4 groups of patients. Normative data were based on 255 neurologically normal adults (aged 18–91 yrs). Clinical groups included 103 patients with severe head trauma, left hemisphere cerebrovascular accident (CVA), right hemisphere CVA, and Alzheimer's disease (mean ages 28.85, 63.46, 64.21, and 64.85 yrs, respectively). Normative data revealed significant age-related differences, with older Ss performing lower on both immediate and delayed recall tasks. Ss in all 4 clinical groups performed significantly below age-matched controls. Visual Reproduction scores correlated positively with measures of visual-spatial ability, verbal memory, and visual memory. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
